-- chem/fock.cub — the small exact universe: the exact matrix of an N-fermion operator H = Σ_i h_i + Σ_{i<j} V_ij given
-- by two tensors on a finite set of orthogonal spin-orbitals, so that a statement about such operators (an inequality,
-- the tightness of a bound, a level) is decided by the machine in a small instance instead of argued by hand.
-- Modes 0..k−1 are spin-orbitals; a basis state is a strictly increasing list of N modes, standing for the
-- antisymmetrised product of its orbitals (`fk-states`). The data: the orbitals' norms d_p (orthogonal, not
-- normalised), h_pq = ⟨p|h|q⟩ and v(p,q,r,s) = ⟨pq|V|rs⟩ (p, r the first particle; q, s the second). The rules
-- (Slater, Condon), from the antisymmetry and the orthogonality, taken here and not proved: with S the modes two states
-- A, B share and D(S) = Π_{q∈S} d_q,
--   A = B:            ⟨A|A⟩ = D(A),  ⟨A|H|A⟩ = D(A)·[Σ_p h_pp/d_p + Σ_{p<q} (v_pqpq − v_pqqp)/(d_p d_q)];
--   one mode differs (a in A, b in B):   ⟨A|H|B⟩ = ±D(S)·[h_ab + Σ_{q∈S} (v_aqbq − v_aqqb)/d_q];
--   two differ (a₁<a₂ in A, b₁<b₂ in B): ⟨A|H|B⟩ = ±D(S)·[v_{a₁a₂b₁b₂} − v_{a₁a₂b₂b₁}];   more: 0;
-- the sign is (−1) to the sum of the positions of the differing modes in A and in B (each differing orbital is brought
-- to the front of its product). One function, `fk-el`, is the entry; `fk-h` and `fk-s` are the matrices.
-- The instance: hydrogen's 1s, 2s, 3s at charge z (chem/onecentre.cub's integrals; 3s added here), each with spin up
-- and down: mode p has orbital ⌊p/2⌋ and spin up when p is even. The tensors are computed once into a table
-- (`fk-tab`) and read from it. Checked: one particle gives hydrogen's levels on the diagonal and nothing else
-- (`fk-va`); the two-electron 1s² entry at z = 2 is −z² + 5z/8 = −11/4 (`fk-vb`); lithium's 1s²2s entry at z = 3 is
-- chem/onecentre.cub's `oc-li` (`fk-vc`); the three-particle matrix is symmetric (`fk-vd`). A level of the pencil
-- (H, S) on any list of states is bracketed by chem/witness.cub's certificate, the search (`fk-find`) outside it.
import "onecentre.cub"
import "witness.cub"

